# The generator writes LF and CI regenerates the cards to compare them against
# what is committed. Without this, a Windows checkout would rewrite them as
# CRLF and every comparison would come out dirty.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touch.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated. Collapse them in diffs and keep them out of language statistics.
cards/*.svg linguist-generated=true
internal/icons/icons.go linguist-generated=true

# Never textually merge the generated output.
#
# Every run of the generator rewrites all of it, so two branches will always
# disagree about it and git will always find a conflict. Left to merge, it
# splices <<<<<<< markers into an SVG and a JSON file, which produces a broken
# snapshot and fourteen broken cards from a merge that touched no source at all.
#
# Unsetting merge makes git keep the current branch's copy and report the
# conflict without editing the file. The fix is then always the same: run the
# generator and commit what it produces.
cards/*.svg -merge
data/snapshot.json -merge
